    {
      "id": "s05",
      "type": "SPEC_COMPARE",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Playwright for Python comes in two flavors, and this trips up almost everybody at the start. Both can do exactly the same things. What differs is purely how much ceremony you have to type around them.",
      "data": {
        "compare": {
          "headline": "Same abilities, different ceremony",
          "a": {
            "name": "sync_api",
            "asset": "lucide:arrow-down"
          },
          "b": {
            "name": "async_api",
            "asset": "lucide:shuffle"
          },
          "rows": [
            {
              "label": "Can do",
              "a": "everything",
              "b": "everything",
              "winner": "tie"
            },
            {
              "label": "Ceremony",
              "a": "none",
              "b": "await",
              "winner": "a"
            },
            {
              "label": "Used for tests",
              "a": "yes",
              "b": "rarely",
              "winner": "a"
            }
          ],
          "atWord": 10.25
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 355,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s05.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "CHAT_MOCKUP",
      "transition": "morph",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Sync is a walkie-talkie conversation. You say one thing. You wait for the reply to come back. Only then do you say the next thing. Nothing else happens while you are waiting, and that simplicity is the entire appeal.",
      "data": {
        "panelLabel": "sync — one at a time",
        "source": "walkie-talkie",
        "messages": [
          {
            "from": "user",
            "text": "open the browser",
            "atWord": 6.417
          },
          {
            "from": "agent",
            "text": "done — waiting on you",
            "atWord": 11
          },
          {
            "from": "user",
            "text": "now go to the page",
            "atWord": 15.667
          },
          {
            "from": "agent",
            "text": "done — waiting on you",
            "atWord": 18.75
          }
        ]
      },
      "durationFrames": 382,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s06.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "BATCH_SWEEP",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Async is a group chat. You fire off several messages at once and handle the replies as they arrive, in whatever order they turn up. Far more powerful when you are driving many pages, and far more wiring to write.",
      "data": {
        "batchSweep": {
          "rows": 6,
          "atWord": 9.833,
          "slow": {
            "label": "One at a time",
            "stat": "sync",
            "color": "blue"
          },
          "fast": {
            "label": "All at once",
            "stat": "async",
            "color": "purple"
          },
          "source": "illustrative"
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 406,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s07.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "type": "THEATER_STAGE",
      "transition": "iris",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "And notice what does not change between the two. Same play, same stage, the same actors standing on the same boards. The only thing that differs is how you choose to direct them from the wings.",
      "data": {
        "stage": {
          "marquee": "the same play",
          "curtain": "up",
          "actors": [
            {
              "label": "a button",
              "kind": "button",
              "atWord": 10.75
            },
            {
              "label": "a text box",
              "kind": "field",
              "atWord": 13.75
            },
            {
              "label": "a link",
              "kind": "link",
              "atWord": 16.75
            }
          ],
          "caption": "only the directing changes",
          "atWord": 5.5
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 345,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s08.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "type": "STICKY_NOTE",
      "transition": "slide",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "So keep this one somewhere. Sync is a walkie-talkie, async is a group chat, and both of them can put on exactly the same show with exactly the same actors.",
      "data": {
        "stickyNote": {
          "headline": "The two flavors",
          "color": "purple",
          "notes": [
            {
              "title": "SYNC vs ASYNC",
              "tag": "memory hook",
              "body": "Sync = walkie-talkie: one at a time, wait for each reply. Async = group chat: many at once, replies as they arrive.",
              "highlight": "Sync = walkie-talkie",
              "asset": "lucide:radio",
              "atWord": 10.917
