    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Here is the sync script from last episode. Look at it closely for a second. There is no await anywhere to be seen, and the whole thing reads straight down the page exactly like ordinary Python does.",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "sync_version.py",
          "language": "py",
          "runLabel": "python sync_version.py",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "# SYNC — what we use in this course",
              "color": "green"
            },
            {
              "text": "from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright"
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "with sync_playwright() as p:"
            },
            {
              "text": "    browser = p.chromium.launch()"
            },
            {
              "text": "    page = browser.new_page()"
            },
            {
              "text": "    page.goto(\"https://playwright.dev\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "    print(page.title())"
            }
          ],
          "atWord": 8.167
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 340,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s11.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "KINETIC_TEXT",
      "transition": "glitch",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Every line finishes completely before the next one is allowed to begin. Which is exactly how Python already feels to you, so there is genuinely nothing new to learn here. That is the whole reason this course uses it.",
      "data": {
        "kinetic": {
          "text": "One line. Then the next.",
          "fx": "typewriter",
          "sub": "no waiting to manage yourself",
          "atWord": 10.583
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 367,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s12.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "transition": "wipe",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "And then the one you only ever need to be able to recognise when you meet it.",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {
          "number": "03",
          "title": "The async flavor",
          "subtitle": "Recognise it, do not fear it"
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 133,
