    {
      "id": "s14",
      "type": "CODE_DIFF",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Here is that very same script in the async flavor, shown as a before and after, so you can see precisely what had to change and, just as importantly, what did not have to change at all.",
      "data": {
        "diff": {
          "fileName": "sync → async",
          "stat": {
            "plus": 4,
            "minus": 2
          },
          "atWord": 7.5,
          "rows": [
            {
              "kind": "del",
              "text": "from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "from playwright.async_api import async_playwright"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "async def main():"
            },
            {
              "kind": "del",
              "text": "    browser = p.chromium.launch()"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "        browser = await p.chromium.launch()"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "asyncio.run(main())"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 310,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s14.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "LIST_BUILD",
      "transition": "morph",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Four changes, and that is the entire difference between the two files. A different import, an async function for it all to live inside, await in front of every single call, and one line at the bottom to start it running.",
      "data": {
        "heading": "Four changes, that is all",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "lucide:package",
            "text": "async_api, not sync_api",
            "detail": "the import changes",
            "atWord": 8.583
          },
          {
            "icon": "lucide:box",
            "text": "everything inside async def",
            "detail": "no more top level",
            "atWord": 13.083
          },
          {
            "icon": "lucide:clock",
            "text": "await in front of every call",
            "detail": "every single one",
            "atWord": 17.667
          },
          {
            "icon": "lucide:play",
            "text": "asyncio.run() at the bottom",
            "detail": "starts it off",
            "atWord": 20.667
          }
        ]
      },
      "durationFrames": 393,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s15.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "transition": "dip",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "That await keyword is the one that matters. It means: send this request off, and let other work carry on in the meantime while we wait for the answer to come back. That is where the overlapping comes from.",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "async_version.py",
          "language": "py",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "async def main():"
            },
            {
              "text": "  async with async_playwright() as p:"
            },
            {
              "text": "    browser = await p.chromium.launch()",
              "color": "purple"
            },
            {
              "text": "    page = await browser.new_page()",
              "color": "purple"
            },
            {
              "text": "    await page.goto(\"https://playwright.dev\")",
              "color": "purple"
            }
          ],
          "atWord": 11.583
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 352,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-03-sync-async_long_s16.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "type": "CHECK_SWEEP",
      "transition": "morph",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Which conveniently gives you a checklist. An async api import, an async def wrapper, await scattered everywhere, and asyncio run down at the bottom. Spot those four tells and you know for certain you are reading async code.",
      "data": {
        "checkSweep": {
          "headline": "The [spot-the-async] checklist",
          "subjectLabel": "the code on screen",
          "checks": [
            {
              "label": "async_api import",
